const commands = [];
for (const command of client.commands.values()) {
    if (typeof command === "function") {
        commands.push({
            name: command.data.name,
            description: command.data.description,
            options: command.data.options,
        });
    }
}
```

Now let's deploy the slash commands:

```TypeScript
async function registerCommands() {
    try {
        await rest.put(
            `/applications/${Config.token}/guilds/<YOUR-GUILD-ID>/commands`,
            { body: commands }
        );
        console.log(chalk.green('Successfully registered application.commands'));
    } catch (error) {
        console.error(error);
    }
}
await registerCommands();
```

We need to update our `deploy.sh` shell script to run `registerCommands` every time we deploy our code changes on staging or production.

Assuming your deployment tool follows a structure like GitLab CI, here's how you'd modify the `deploy.sh` shell script:

```bash
